WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:09.980
So get it out of their heads.

2
00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:11.480
That’s the Playbook.

3
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:19.080
Take Oriva,

4
00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.120
a coffee roaster.

5
00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:27.860
But only the two founders

6
00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:28.780
know it.

7
00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:30.200
They told the team once,

8
00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.200
and a week later

9
00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:32.000
a post went out

10
00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:32.720
in the old

11
00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.080
brown colours.

12
00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:35.000
Tell them again,

13
00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:35.620
louder?

14
00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:36.580
No.

15
00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:38.500
People forget what they’re told.

16
00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:40.500
They follow what they can look up.

17
00:00:47.289 --> 00:00:48.989
The founders’ first draft:

18
00:00:49.629 --> 00:00:50.129
premium,

19
00:00:50.169 --> 00:00:50.689
friendly,

20
00:00:50.969 --> 00:00:51.529
fresh.

21
00:00:55.249 --> 00:00:56.209
So every rule

22
00:00:56.249 --> 00:00:57.389
gets an example.

23
00:01:01.989 --> 00:01:03.349
But people write the posts,

24
00:01:03.389 --> 00:01:05.149
and people drift.

25
00:01:10.153 --> 00:01:11.393
Last month’s posts:

26
00:01:11.893 --> 00:01:12.633
premium quality,

27
00:01:12.673 --> 00:01:14.333
artisanal.

28
00:01:14.373 --> 00:01:15.853
Every rival says that.

29
00:01:21.753 --> 00:01:22.293
But who checks

30
00:01:22.333 --> 00:01:23.513
before it goes out?

31
00:01:23.807 --> 00:01:25.327
So the Company Guidebook

32
00:01:25.367 --> 00:01:26.147
puts the brand

33
00:01:26.187 --> 00:01:27.527
into daily work,

34
00:01:27.767 --> 00:01:28.667
role by role.

35
00:01:28.787 --> 00:01:30.407
Every role gets its pages,

36
00:01:30.627 --> 00:01:32.227
from the roaster to the driver.

37
00:01:32.647 --> 00:01:34.447
New hires learn it in week one.

38
00:01:34.807 --> 00:01:36.367
And the step most teams skip:

39
00:01:36.747 --> 00:01:37.447
approval.

40
00:01:37.687 --> 00:01:38.687
That brown post?

41
00:01:38.947 --> 00:01:40.547
This is where it gets caught.

42
00:01:40.827 --> 00:01:41.647
But outside,

43
00:01:41.687 --> 00:01:42.667
the founders pitch Oriva

44
00:01:42.707 --> 00:01:43.847
two different ways.

45
00:01:44.169 --> 00:01:45.929
So the story is written once,

46
00:01:45.969 --> 00:01:47.469
and shaped for every room.

47
00:01:53.789 --> 00:01:54.749
And the roastery walls

48
00:01:54.789 --> 00:01:56.529
tell it to every visitor.

49
00:01:56.929 --> 00:01:58.649
But where does it all live?

50
00:01:59.104 --> 00:02:00.704
That’s the Deliverables:

51
00:02:00.964 --> 00:02:02.104
how it’s handed over.

52
00:02:02.444 --> 00:02:03.984
A playbook nobody can find

53
00:02:04.024 --> 00:02:04.924
is a playbook

54
00:02:04.964 --> 00:02:06.224
nobody uses.

55
00:02:06.751 --> 00:02:08.271
Remember the brown post?

56
00:02:08.631 --> 00:02:09.911
It came from an old template

57
00:02:09.951 --> 00:02:11.231
in the shared drive.

58
00:02:11.511 --> 00:02:12.871
So the old files go,

59
00:02:12.911 --> 00:02:13.851
and it’s handed

60
00:02:13.891 --> 00:02:15.211
over three ways:

61
00:02:15.551 --> 00:02:16.531
a printed book,

62
00:02:16.871 --> 00:02:18.111
an online portal,

63
00:02:18.451 --> 00:02:19.771
one tidy folder.

64
00:02:20.251 --> 00:02:21.351
Now everyone,

65
00:02:21.391 --> 00:02:22.271
even the printer,

66
00:02:22.311 --> 00:02:23.751
opens the latest version.

67
00:02:27.666 --> 00:02:28.866
So, how do you get a brand

68
00:02:28.906 --> 00:02:30.166
out of two heads?

69
00:02:30.586 --> 00:02:31.786
Not by saying it louder.

70
00:02:32.246 --> 00:02:33.566
You write it down

71
00:02:33.606 --> 00:02:34.326
where everyone

72
00:02:34.366 --> 00:02:35.506
can look it up.

73
00:02:37.746 --> 00:02:38.366
Nothing went out

74
00:02:38.406 --> 00:02:39.366
in the old colours.

75
00:02:39.881 --> 00:02:40.761
But café owners

76
00:02:40.801 --> 00:02:42.341
still visit the site,

77
00:02:42.381 --> 00:02:42.801
look around,

78
00:02:42.841 --> 00:02:43.781
and leave.

79
00:02:44.281 --> 00:02:45.361
Why don’t they buy?

80
00:02:45.741 --> 00:02:48.767
That’s Conversion.

